{"name":"Baby Bunting","hex":"#abcaea","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"baby","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A very young human, particularly from birth to a couple of years old or until walking is fully mastered.","Any very young animal, especially a vertebrate; many species have specific names for their babies, such as kittens for the babies of cats, puppies for the babies of dogs, and chicks for the babies of birds. See Category:Baby animals for more."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Picked when small and immature (as in baby corn, baby potatoes).","Newest (overall, or in some group or state); most inexperienced."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/baby"},{"term":"bunting","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Strips of material used as festive decoration, especially in the colours of the national flag.","A thin cloth of woven wool from which flags are made; it is light enough to spread in a gentle wind but resistant to fraying in a strong wind."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of various songbirds of the genus Emberiza, having short bills and brown or gray plumage."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bunting"}],"entries":[{"title":"Baby Bunting","blocks":[{"text":"Baby Bunting Group Limited is an Australian baby products retail chain. Its stores, located across Australia but with a focus on Australia's eastern coast, sell baby and children's clothing and items."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Baby_Bunting%2C_Cannington.jpg/330px-Baby_Bunting%2C_Cannington.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Baby_Bunting","wikidata":"Q109626935"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/46/Baby_Bunting%2C_Cannington.jpg/500px-Baby_Bunting%2C_Cannington.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimed